WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.033
Compute frontiers.

2
00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:06.667
Three post GPU ideas, and they are closer to production than quantum.

3
00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:09.433
All three attack one wall.

4
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:11.000
Weights sit in memory.

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:16.000
Moving data to the compute unit costs more energy than the arithmetic itself.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.037
Then the results travel back.

7
00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:20.133
That memory wall is the motivation.

8
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:26.500
First, neuromorphic chips, like Intel Loihi, IBM NorthPole and SpiNNaker.

9
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.167
They compute with sparse spikes instead of dense clocked matrix multiplies.

10
00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:34.200
Spiking networks do not train with plain backprop.

11
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.067
Power is extremely low, ideal for always on sensing.

12
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.057
The blocker is software.

13
00:00:40.057 --> 00:00:42.733
No PyTorch scale ecosystem exists yet.

14
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:45.700
Second, photonic computing.

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.533
Light carries the numbers in.

16
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:55.133
As it passes through interferometers, the matrix multiplication simply happens, with no heat from the multiply itself.

17
00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:57.467
A detector reads out the answer.

18
00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.900
In datacenters, light between chips is arriving first.

19
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.667
Here is how the three stand.

20
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:07.367
Neuromorphic and photonic compute are on the watch list.

21
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:12.785
Analog in memory compute is the one most likely to reach edge AI products soon.

22
00:01:12.785 --> 00:01:18.033
It multiplies inside the memory array, though precision and drift are challenges.

23
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:20.533
So what should you do now?

24
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:21.861
Nothing but read.

25
00:01:21.861 --> 00:01:25.367
None of this changes your daily work in twenty twenty six.

26
00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:27.319
Let's recap.

27
00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.700
The memory wall is the shared problem.

28
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.700
Neuromorphic means spikes and low power, but no software yet.

29
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.200
Photonic uses light for matrix math and links.

30
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.457
Analog in memory is likeliest at the edge.

31
00:01:40.457 --> 00:01:43.133
Next up: embodied AI and world models.
